    "body": "How to use it in our team (read first): you work inside the team app, not in a code editor. You cannot run scripts, install packages, open a browser or a terminal – skip every step that needs them and apply the rules yourself. Deliver pages with make_file (one self-contained HTML file, Hebrew, RTL, mobile first, dark mode), new images with make_image (each one waits for the owner's approval and costs about $0.04 – propose only the few that matter) and place them with {{file:<id>}}. Our built-in design system rules (design-system) still apply. Source: github.com/VoltAgent/awesome-design-md (MIT license).\n\nA collection of 84 DESIGN.md files – the design language of well-known sites (colors, typography, spacing, components, rules), written for AI agents to build consistent UI.\n1. Pick the brand whose style fits the request (or the one the owner named). Available: 1win, airbnb, airtable, aljazeera, apple, binance, bmw, bmw-m, bugatti, cal, claude, clay, clickhouse, cohere, coinbase, composio, cursor, dell-1996, dji, elevenlabs, expo, ferrari, figma, framer, hashicorp, hp, ibm, intercom, jobright, kraken, lamborghini, linear.app, lovable, mastercard, mercury, meta, minimax, mintlify, miro, mistral.ai, mongodb, mydealz, nerdwallet, nike, nintendo-2001, notion, nvidia, ollama, opencode.ai, oracle, oura, pinterest, playstation, posthog, raycast, renault, replicate, resend, revolut, runwayml, sanity, sap, sentry, shopify, slack, spacex, spotify, starbucks, stripe, supabase, superhuman, tesla, theverge, together.ai, uber, vercel, vodafone, voltagent, warp, webflow, wired, wise, x.ai, zapier.\n2. Fetch its file with web_fetch: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VoltAgent/awesome-design-md/main/design-md/<name>/DESIGN.md\n3. Build with that design language (tokens, type scale, spacing, component style) – adapted to Hebrew/RTL and to the owner's own brand name, logo and content. Inspired by, never a copy: no other company's logo, name or text.\n4. Tell the owner in one line which design language you used."
